<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:56Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Human trafficking victims stranded in Guinea-Bissau</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c04147ecd951e665dd57c764e38c2b2a6c06b817b7f0cf5df2baf80cee43c9e</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558--af9688fcc3e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/human-trafficking-victims-stranded-in-guinea-bissau/a-79785558?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Dozens of West Africans lured to Guinea-Bissau with promises of jobs and migration to Europe say they were exploited by a suspected trafficking network. Now many cannot afford to return home.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Can EU and India work together to secure Indo-Pacific?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04537ee63c62def2c9e0e15fcb56aa17e47dd8d3b4dc5e6de3f764437d443745</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-eu-and-india-work-together-to-secure-indo-pacific/a-79796195--03242e3284fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-eu-and-india-work-together-to-secure-indo-pacific/a-79796195?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India and Europe are deepening defense ties, but their clashing perspectives on Russia and differing priorities on China are hampering their joint ambitions on maritime security.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>European Central Bank (ECB) head Christine Lagarde to step down in February, before her term ends</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21de815797c0727d8bc12dbb87edcbf79d7c7b3f42302c1f0b9c5372a5ab08b1</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-central-bank-ecb-head-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-before-her-term-ends/a-79794353--c27511a3878b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-central-bank-ecb-head-christine-lagarde-to-step-down-in-february-before-her-term-ends/a-79794353?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">European Central Bank (ECB) President Christine Lagarde is to resign nine months ahead of the end of her 8-year term. European Council President Antonio Costa has said the process to find a successor is underway.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ship reported on fire off Oman as Iran escalation fears mount</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bfed07dce2c75fd655e4f7f15417c4bdf6f43a772b2a807fbc0b01b6371a361d</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:19:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T10:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ship-reported-on-fire-off-oman-as-iran-escalation-fears-mount/a-79792733--778ab60c5f97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ship-reported-on-fire-off-oman-as-iran-escalation-fears-mount/a-79792733?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A ship in the Strait of Hormuz is reported to be on fire, a British maritime agency says. Iran has meanwhile said it has shot down another US drone as military tensions with Washington continue.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Flavio Bolsonaro lands in US, declares himself 'leader' of Brazil</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6a1fd404b93bd4e114e5f5897909f26fe382dfbce9e1a015f7f1ee3f473f4ee4</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T22:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-us-declares-himself-leader-of-brazil/a-79788659--e413c3c7c69a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/flavio-bolsonaro-lands-in-us-declares-himself-leader-of-brazil/a-79788659?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Flavio Bolsonaro declared himself the rightful leader of his country despite losing the presidential election runoff on Sunday. He and his family have fled to the US.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: What you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:695a40674df49780b5dd33f287c96e0e431799014a13bc09629ea8ed5ee43841</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T19:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-do-the-us-midterms-work-and-why-are-they-so-important-for-trump-s-presidency/a-79789932--5c980e8318e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-what-you-need-to-know/a-79789932?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US voters are electing a new Congress. The results will be decisive for the future of the United States, and a judgment on Donald Trump's second term as president.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Evacuation from Oleshky: How are preparations going?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb9acb5fc1d53f20f5cad70d2842f4f655929e21627cfbaa6a50643da23a67c9</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T17:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/evacuation-from-oleshky-how-are-preparations-going/a-79790001--e77f75613f06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/evacuation-from-oleshky-how-are-preparations-going/a-79790001?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A lawyer with the Save Ukraine Foundation, Myroslava Kharchenko, told DW about what has been happening in Russian-occupied Oleshky since a temporary ceasefire brokered by Melania Trump took effect.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>One year on, families seek justice after election violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7eaae61250c01c1d8a86443f20160a7a299e5ec6875b10ddc25fc7d5666ecdd</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/one-year-on-families-seek-justice-after-election-violence/a-79779105--19ee0afa750b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/one-year-on-families-seek-justice-after-election-violence/a-79779105?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One year after Tanzania's deadly post-election violence, families are still seeking answers. A government inquiry recorded 518 deaths. DW research has documented apparent use of excessive force by security forces.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What would a new Israeli government mean for Arab neighbors? More of the same is expected, with some small positives predicted.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f54c145f23cd61f0b8affcd3e0af03bb6e5422a11fa31267508544c66170deb</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T16:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-would-a-new-israeli-government-mean-for-arab-neighbors-more-of-the-same-is-expected-with-some-s/a-79788174--4047f4a42d4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-would-a-new-israeli-government-mean-for-arab-neighbors-more-of-the-same-is-expected-with-some-small-positives-predicted/a-79788174?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new Israeli government is unlikely to bring big changes on Palestinian statehood and troops in Lebanon and Syria, experts say. Some small positives may be possible though.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran headed to war or peace after Mecca alliance meeting?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac69c226afde442037838f4bdf00755a2ed2f7de8ff28738fe19855bf63595b4</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256--9ef674df50a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey have taken their latest peace push directly to Tehran. Officially, it was to avert a new military escalation, but their diplomatic outreach can also be seen as a warning to Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU's 'Made in Europe' push unnerves global auto suppliers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a57dfdada279f7d67e5511c74e1270b0b65b88633a701ad1aef3a87796bef87</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T10:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579--7391c1bc1a80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-s-made-in-europe-push-unnerves-global-auto-suppliers/a-79732579?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In shielding Europe's carmakers from Chinese rivals, the EU risks hurting close partners from Turkey and Morocco to Japan and South Korea. Billions in trade and hundreds of thousands of European jobs are at stake.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Russia in Africa: What is Putin hoping to achieve?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d5b18fa8442021fca9f74678ac0078112e10763e5ec2e337bc613bbf26d83ab</id><updated>2026-10-29T15:18:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T09:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858--24074440aebf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-in-africa-what-is-putin-hoping-to-achieve/a-79781858?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following its invasion of Ukraine and the resulting rift with the West, Russia has declared that it intends to make a "historic return" to Africa. What have we seen of this so far?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
